---
/**
 * The model in plain words: work, agents, decisions, evidence, playbooks,
 * pods and budgets, one section each (src/content/docs/model).
 */
import DocPage from "../components/DocPage.astro";
import NextStep from "../components/NextStep.astro";
import { href, SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<DocPage
  page="model"
  title="How vyuha works"
  heading="The model, in plain words."
  eyebrow="The model"
  description="How vyuha works in plain words: work, agents, decisions, evidence, playbooks, pods and budgets, and how they let a small team run a company of agents."
  image="/og/model.png"
  imageAlt="vyuha, the model: work, agents, decisions, evidence, playbooks, pods and budgets."
>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    Seven ideas explain vyuha. Work is what you track. Agents do it. Decisions say what they may do
    alone. Evidence shows what they did. Playbooks, pods and budgets give the company its shape.
  </Fragment>
  <NextStep
    title="See the first steps."
    primary={{ label: "Read the getting-started guide", href: href("/guide/") }}
    secondary={{ label: "Request access on GitHub", href: SITE.accessRequest, external: true }}
  >
    The guide covers what you do once you have access: connect a repository, create a project, file
    a first issue and read a run's evidence.
  </NextStep>
</DocPage>
